            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0812" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/805: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-14T14:00:00+07:00">June 14, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 1410:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1028. Drumright reports from Sian in telegram June 10 he is informed that,
                    evidently in connection with general withdrawal of Russian military advisers,
                    those to 8th War Area, Sian, were departing that day for Russia. In despatch
                    June 7 Penfield in Chengtu states 6 Soviet military aviation advisers left there
                    June 6 en route to Russia on expiration of contracts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
